# Staged build inputs -- see scripts/stage-assets.mjs.
#
# Everything under public/ is either copied from elsewhere in the repo
# (../checkpoints/, node_modules/onnxruntime-web/dist/) or downloaded and
# checksummed. Tracking a second copy of a 6.2 MB model is how the two get out
# of sync, and the digest check in the staging script only helps if there is
# one original.
#
# These rules live HERE and not in public/.gitignore for a reason that cost a
# deploy: Vite copies public/ into dist/ verbatim, dotfiles included. A
# .gitignore in public/ therefore lands in dist/ -- where it both gets served
# as part of the site and, because the publish step commits dist/ to a branch,
# silently filters the deployment down to the handful of files it happened to
# whitelist. The symptom was a live site consisting of one JSON file.
public/*
!public/models/
public/models/*

# The exception. Generating models.json needs torch + onnxruntime, because it
# verifies that each ONNX export really is the checkpoint its accuracy figures
# were measured on. Making CI install a deep-learning stack to publish a static
# site is not worth it, so the file is committed and a server test
# (test_static_registry.py) fails if it has drifted from server/.
!public/models/models.json
